+# Retiring `legacy_db.query_raw`
+
+Migration plan for moving off `app/legacy_db.py` onto `app/db/session.py`.
+
+## Call sites
+
+- `app/orders/service.py` — imports `query_raw` from `app.legacy_db` and uses it for both order reads (`open_orders`) and writes (`cancel`).
+- `app/billing/invoices.py` — imports the `app.legacy_db` module and calls `legacy_db.query_raw` to read unpaid invoices for a customer.
+- `app/admin/tools.py` — imports `query_raw` as `qr` and calls it to delete test customers.
+
+## Schema
+
+Current schema version: 14
+
+This migration does not need a new schema version. It is a code-level swap of
+the connection layer only and changes no tables or indexes. The next version
+number (15) is already reserved for a separate follow-up: dropping the legacy
+views once `legacy_db` is fully gone.
+
+## Environment
+
+- `ORDERS_DB_URL` — read by `app/settings.py` (required; `os.environ[...]`); used as the connection URL. The new session layer still needs it (`Session` defaults to `settings.DB_URL`).
+- `ORDERS_DB_POOL` — read by `app/settings.py` as `DB_POOL_SIZE` (default `5`). The new session layer still needs it (`Session` defaults to `settings.DB_POOL_SIZE`).
+- `LEGACY_DB_TIMEOUT_S` — read by `app/legacy_db.py` (default `30`) as the old driver's connect timeout. The new session layer does not use it; it can be dropped once `legacy_db` is removed.
+- `BILLING_CURRENCY` — read by `app/billing/invoices.py` via `app/util/env.env` (default `EUR`) for invoice output formatting. Unrelated to the connection layer and still needed after the switch.
+
+## Rollback
+
+The switch is a wiring change, not a data migration, so rollback is a revert.
+Land it behind a single deployable change so we can back it out without a
+schema step:
+
+1. Keep `app/legacy_db.py` in the tree and untouched until the new code has run
+   in production; do not delete it in the same change that switches callers.
+2. If the switch misbehaves, revert the commit(s) that repoint the call sites to
+   `app/db/session.py` and redeploy. The legacy path becomes active again with
+   no database action required, since no schema version was consumed.
+3. Only delete `legacy_db.py` and start the version 15 work (dropping the legacy
+   views) once the session layer has been stable in production.
